OL,3,GNEWSAAsbestos-hit beach set to remain
OL,4,Ashut for months
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn asbestos-hit beach is expected to
OL,7,Fremain shut for several months while
OL,8,Fexperts determine the source of
OL,9,Fcontamination.
OL,11,FMount Batten beach in Plymouth, Devon,
OL,12,Fremains closed after "high levels of
OL,13,Fasbestos fibres" were found in the sand
OL,14,Fin July.
OL,16,FPlymouth City Council said it was "in
OL,17,Fthe process of commissioning specialist
OL,18,Fconsultants to carry out further
OL,19,Finvestigations" with options for making
OL,20,Fthe beach "safe to open" expected in
OL,21,Fthe spring.
OL,23,APub: 06-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
